  "question": {
    "text": "$\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}}\\left(x^{n} \\ln x\\right), n>0$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "IPGJo",
      "text": "does not exist",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "VWqw6",
      "text": "exists and is zero",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3ajkM",
      "text": "exists and is 1",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gvIPT",
      "text": "exists and is $e^{-1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have,\r\n$\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}} x^{n} \\ln x$\r\n$=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}} \\frac{\\ln x}{x^{-n}}$\r\n$=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}} \\frac{x}{-n x^{-n-1}} \\quad$ [using L'Hospital's rule $]$\r\n$=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}} \\frac{-1}{n x^{-n}}=0 \\quad\\left[\\because \\frac{1}{x-n}=0,\\right.$ when $\\left.x=0\\right]$",
    "image": null
  },
